+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-21-reject-undefined-patch-value/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` validates `value` with `has(operation, "value")`, which is true for an own property holding `undefined`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** reject `undefined` values like missing ones.
+**Non-Goals:** other behaviour is already RFC 6902 conformant and is unchanged (including `remove` of the root being an error).
+
+## Decisions
+
+Extend the existing check to `!has(operation, "value") || operation.value === undefined`, reusing the "needs a value" error. No new error type.
